# Gate step 1650-fb7z — the preflight door removes a stale .git/index.lock that
# a guard's git left, and only such a lock. A git SIGKILLed while it holds the
# lock (proc.run's timeout_ms KILLs the group; the Lua guard then ends on its
# own) runs no cleanup. build.sh's _pf_run_guard and _pf_sweep_late are
# extracted against a scratch git repository: the trunk door (both sweep calls
# removed) leaves the lock, the fixed door removes it and names it, and a lock
# a live process holds, or one older than the run, is never removed.
#
# STEP_LUA is a LITERAL path on purpose (1063-nraf).
STEP_DESC="Checking the door sweeps a stale index.lock a killed git left, and never a held one (1650-fb7z)"
STEP_LUA="scripts/lua/test-door-index-lock-sweep.lua"
STEP_ERROR="the preflight door no longer removes a stale index.lock a killed git left, or removed one a live process holds or one older than the run (1650-fb7z) — see the FAIL lines above"
STEP_OK="Door index-lock sweep fixture passed"
# 1765-q7rg: the sweep races a killed git under host load, so one red is
# retried once after a settle and a second reads flaky:.
STEP_HOST_STATE="load"
STEP_SECOND_REGIME="yolanda-windows 2026-10-13 msys ok:door-index-lock-sweep:8 arms"
